# Indobase production redeploy (Vyom / indobase.in)

Use this when the user asks to **deploy**, ship to **prod**, or roll out on **Vyom**. Default working branch is **`main`**. Do not route through `staging` / `indobase.fun`.

## 1. Source of truth

- **Repo branch:** `main` on GitHub (`Indobase/Indobase`).
- **CI:** Push to `main` triggers `.github/workflows/docker-publish.yml` → Docker Hub `roshanraghavander/ind-repo:<sha>`, `roshanraghavander/indobase-builder:<sha>`, and `roshanraghavander/indobase-builder-cfos:<sha>`.
- Prefer the **commit SHA** tag for rollout (not `:latest`).

## 2. Git

- Commit on `main`, then **`git push origin main`**.
- Before pushing `main`: `git fetch origin` and integrate if behind (`git pull --rebase origin main`).
- `SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)` on `main` after that push.
- Do not force-push.

## 3. VPS rollout (Docker Swarm)

- **Control-plane:** `root@103.190.92.249` (Studio + Builder CFOS + platform Postgres)
- **Tenant data-plane:** `root@103.190.92.248` (provisioner + tenant stacks)
- **SSH key:** `~/.ssh/id_ed25519_indobase_vps`
- **CFOS Builder:** `IMAGE_TAG=<SHA> ./docker/scripts/deploy-indobase-builder-cfos-on-vps.sh`
- **Studio:** on `.249`, `docker service ls --format '{{.Name}}' | grep -E 'indobase-studio' | head -1`

1. Wait for Hub tag(s) HTTP 200.
2. On `.249`: pull image(s), `docker service update --image …`, run `indobase-studio-attach-compose-network.sh` after Studio updates.
3. Verify Studio: `curl -sS https://studio.indobase.in/api/health/live` → `version` == `<SHA>`.
4. Verify CFOS: `curl -sS https://builder.indobase.in/sso/health` → `version` == `<SHA>`.

Do **not** deploy Studio/Builder to Hostinger `187.77.30.165` or `72.61.242.251` unless the user explicitly names `indobase.fun`.

## 4. Docs

- Prod secrets/Dokploy: `docker/DOKPLOY-STUDIO-DEPLOY.md`
